    "hypothesis": "Demo-pashley's silent-letter/soft-sound chunking strategy, reinforced with a second teach-plus-untimed-practice cycle, now generalizes to the gn- pattern (gnat) and the ci→/sh pattern (special): both are spelled correctly, unaided, on an independent fresh checkpoint after reverting once before. The wr-, kn-, -mb, and ci→/s patterns, plus the 11 originally-known words, continue to hold steady with no fatigue cost. However, 'building' — previously fixed and confirmed correct three times — reverted once to 'bilding' on the newest, stricter timed (8s) hidden-word, whole-word-input checkpoint, which provided no per-item response time to evaluate whether this was a genuine lapse or a speed/format-pressure artifact (consistent with an earlier timed-mechanic slip on a different word). The theory is revised to withhold judgment on 'building' specifically until one more untimed retrieval rep and one more fresh, independent checkpoint are observed, rather than either re-teaching it from scratch or declaring the full word set consolidated.",
